; Entity handler: Death's scythe sliding along a floor
;
; Second state of the scythe (see #R$BAB1, which sets it when the scythe lands). The signed x speed in slot +2 is
; added to x ($FF80 moves the scythe left, $0080 right). It disappears (#R$BADF) when x is $71 or more or less than 8
; (2-pixel units, the edges of the room) or when a cell under it is harmful. If the cells under its lower edge have no
; solid flag the floor has ended and the handler word goes back to #R$BAB1 (it falls again); otherwise it is drawn.
; .
; Slot layout: see #R$BAB1.
; .
; Bug candidate: the drawing path at $BB50 (a solid cell under the scythe: with the scythe at its rounded height that
; only happens when it slides into a ledge or wall) loads D and E from the x position, because H holds x here and not
; y, so the scythe would be drawn at y = x. It was not reached in any run, so the bug is not observed; the usual path
; (#R$BAB1 and this routine alternating, see the findings) draws through #R$BB02.
;
; SP Slot address + 2 (the handler word was popped by the RET that entered the routine)
@label=UpdateScytheSliding
c$BB07 POP BC        ; x speed
 $BB08 POP DE        ; y speed (not used)
 $BB09 POP HL        ; x
 $BB0A ADD HL,BC     ; x moves
 $BB0B PUSH HL       ; store x
 $BB0C EXX           ;
 $BB0D POP DE        ; D' = x word
 $BB0E EXX           ;
 $BB0F POP DE        ; y word
 $BB10 LD A,D        ; A = y
 $BB11 EXX           ;
 $BB12 ADD A,$07     ; cell row of the lower edge, as a word index
 $BB14 RRA           ;
 $BB15 AND $3E       ;
 $BB17 LD L,A        ;
 $BB18 LD H,$61      ; row address table at $6100
 $BB1A LD A,D        ; x in 2-pixel units
 $BB1B CP $71        ; right edge of the room
 $BB1D JR NC,$BADF   ;
 $BB1F CP $08        ; left edge
 $BB21 JR C,$BADF    ;
 $BB23 LD C,A        ; byte column and cell address as in #R$BAB1
 $BB24 RRA           ;
 $BB25 RRA           ;
 $BB26 AND $1F       ;
 $BB28 ADD A,(HL)    ;
 $BB29 INC L         ;
 $BB2A LD H,(HL)     ;
 $BB2B LD L,A        ;
 $BB2C LD A,C        ;
 $BB2D AND $03       ;
 $BB2F JR Z,$BB33    ;
 $BB31 LD A,(HL)     ;
 $BB32 INC L         ;
*$BB33 OR (HL)       ;
 $BB34 INC L         ;
 $BB35 OR (HL)       ;
 $BB36 BIT 2,A       ; harmful?
 $BB38 JR NZ,$BADF   ;
 $BB3A AND $03       ; solid cell under it: stay in this state
 $BB3C JR NZ,$BB50   ;
 $BB3E LD HL,$FFF8   ; no floor: back to falling
 $BB41 ADD HL,SP     ;
 $BB42 LD SP,HL      ;
 $BB43 LD HL,$BAB1   ; new handler: falling
 $BB46 PUSH HL       ; written over the handler word at slot+0
 $BB47 POP HL        ;
 $BB48 EXX           ;
 $BB49 POP BC        ; pop x speed, y speed, x and y again
 $BB4A POP BC        ;
 $BB4B POP DE        ;
 $BB4C POP HL        ;
 $BB4D LD A,D        ;
 $BB4E JR $BB02      ;
*$BB50 LD A,D        ; see the description: D and E both get x
 $BB51 EXX           ;
 $BB52 LD D,H        ;
 $BB53 LD E,A        ;
 $BB54 JP $B9BE      ;
